## Day 5 — Run & full manual test

```powershell
docker compose up -d --build
docker compose exec app pytest -q
```

Then in the browser at `http://localhost:8000/docs`, run the **whole flow by hand**:
1. `POST /datasets/upload?name=orders` with a CSV → note the `dataset_id`.
2. `POST /rules` a few times to define the contract for `orders`
   (e.g. `customer_id` not_null, `amount` positive, `status` in_set).
3. `POST /datasets/{id}/validate`.
4. `GET /datasets/{id}/report` → see counts + health score + most common error.
5. `GET /datasets/{id}/quarantine` → see the bad rows with reasons.

**Checkpoint:** the entire pipeline works end to end through the API. This is the
core Semester-1 deliverable functioning.

